  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive nucleus decays by two different processes. The half-life for the first process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and that for the second is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The effective half-life of the nucleus is close to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0097_84baa08f3c14.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 120px;\" /></p><p>Using the equation of radioactive decay&nbsp;law,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Where,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is the rate of decay</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are decay constant for two different processes</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math>&nbsp;is the number&nbsp;of atoms.</p><p>Now applying the decay law for the combine process, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mi>N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Equating equation (1) and (2) we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now the half life of the radioactive nucleus is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;is the&nbsp;half life of the radioactive nucleus</p><p>Using equation (5) equation (4) becomes,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p>"
  }
}